exports[`every document, every preset > strict > snapshot: agent brief 1`] = `
"Moderation policy for Strict (generated by Chatwarden)
Summary: Be kind. No swearing, insults or bullying.

RULES
CR 1. No slurs or hate aimed at who someone is: Do not use slurs, or put someone down for their race, religion, gender, sexuality, disability or similar. This applies to what you say about other players and about anyone else.
CR 2. No insulting, threatening or targeting another player: Do not insult, swear at, threaten or target another player in chat. Talking about the game itself is fine; aiming it at a person is not.
CR 3. No sexual messages: Do not send sexual messages or comments, and do not pressure anyone for them.
CR 4. No spam, flooding or advertising: Do not repeat the same message, flood the chat or advertise. Stick to talking about the game and the people in it.
CR 5. No cheating or exploiting: Do not cheat, or use a bug or loophole to get an unfair edge. Report bugs instead of using them.
CR 6. No throwing, stalling or ruining games on purpose: Do not lose on purpose, stall the game or leave a game running just to spoil it for others. Play to finish, or concede.
CR 7. No offensive names: Do not pick a name that breaks any other rule here, such as a slur, a sexual name or a name aimed at another player.
CR 8. No false reports: Do not report someone to get them in trouble when they have not broken a rule. Use reports for real problems.

CONDUCT LEVELS
banter: Friendly salt and jokes about play, with no insults and no swearing (examples: ez; gg; bad play; lol)
rude: Any insult or swearing aimed at a player, even once (examples: loser; you're an idiot; go f— yourself)
hostile: Sustained or repeated aggression: several insults, picking a fight, following someone across games (examples: three insults in one game; insulting the same player again next game)
severe: Threats, hate or slurs, attacks on who someone is, sexual harassment, doxxing, serious harassment (examples: any slur; I'll find you; anything about race or religion as an attack)

OUTCOMES
First offense, with a clean record:
- banter: No action
- rude: Restrict chat 1 hour
- hostile: Restrict chat 24 hours
- severe: Full ban 7 days
Repeated: 1 note in 30 days counts as repeated: Restrict chat 24 hours. Applies only while the record holds no warning or restriction, and is never milder than the first offense.
Record steps: 0 is notes only, 1 is a warning, 2 is a chat or area restriction under 7 days (or two warnings), 3 is a restriction of 7 days or more or a ban under 7 days, 4 is a ban of 7 to 29 days, 5 is a ban of 30 days or more or anything permanent.
Escalation after the first offense. Step = heaviest action on the record in the last 90 days. Low = banter and rude; high = hostile once the record has a warning or restriction, and severe:
- step 0: low Warning | high Restrict chat 7 days
- step 1: low Restrict chat 24 hours | high Restrict chat 7 days
- step 2: low Restrict chat 7 days | high Full ban 7 days
- step 3: low Full ban 7 days | high Full ban 30 days
- step 4: low Full ban 30 days | high Full ban permanent
- step 5: low Full ban permanent | high Full ban permanent
A chat restriction becomes a ban from public rooms and matchmaking (same length) for: CR 5, CR 6.
Always read the high column for: CR 1.
Guidelines:
- Banter (covers: banter): No action. Nothing is recorded.
- Rudeness (covers: rude, repeated behaviour): First time: chat restricted for 1 hour. Repeated (any earlier note on the record): chat restricted for 24 hours.
- Bullying (covers: hostile): Chat restricted for 24 hours.
- After a warning (covers: after a warning): Longer restrictions, then bans, stepping up with each action.
- Severe (covers: severe): A 7 day ban at once.
Profanity: refuse. The profanity filter never creates a strike, note, sanction or notice. Swearing aimed at a player is still judged as rude.

AI AUTO-ACT
The AI may act on its own for: hostile, severe. Auto-act is never banter or rude; a moderator decides those.
Standard for the AI read: This is a game for younger players and families, and the aim is a kind space. Read only friendly salt and jokes about play ("ez", "gg", "bad play") as banter, and take no action; swearing that is not aimed at anyone is stopped before it is sent and is not a violation. Read any insult or swearing aimed at a player, even a mild one such as "loser", as rude. Read several insults, bullying, picking a fight or following someone across games as hostile. Read threats, hate, slurs, attacks on who someone is, sexual harassment and doxxing as severe. Judge the pattern across the reported lines, and when unsure choose the milder level.
"
`;

exports[`every document, every preset > strict > snapshot: code of conduct (markdown) 1`] = `
"# Example Game code of conduct

Be kind. No swearing, insults or bullying.

## The rules

- **CR 1. No slurs or hate aimed at who someone is**: Do not use slurs, or put someone down for their race, religion, gender, sexuality, disability or similar. This applies to what you say about other players and about anyone else.
- **CR 2. No insulting, threatening or targeting another player**: Do not insult, swear at, threaten or target another player in chat. Talking about the game itself is fine; aiming it at a person is not.
- **CR 3. No sexual messages**: Do not send sexual messages or comments, and do not pressure anyone for them.
- **CR 4. No spam, flooding or advertising**: Do not repeat the same message, flood the chat or advertise. Stick to talking about the game and the people in it.
- **CR 5. No cheating or exploiting**: Do not cheat, or use a bug or loophole to get an unfair edge. Report bugs instead of using them.
- **CR 6. No throwing, stalling or ruining games on purpose**: Do not lose on purpose, stall the game or leave a game running just to spoil it for others. Play to finish, or concede.
- **CR 7. No offensive names**: Do not pick a name that breaks any other rule here, such as a slur, a sexual name or a name aimed at another player.
- **CR 8. No false reports**: Do not report someone to get them in trouble when they have not broken a rule. Use reports for real problems.

## What happens if you break a rule

What happens depends on what you did and on whether it has happened before. Reported messages are reviewed before a decision is made.

### Banter

**What counts:** Friendly salt and jokes about play, with no insults and no swearing.

**What happens:**

- Nothing happens.

For example: "ez", "gg", "bad play", "lol".

### Rudeness

**What counts:** Any insult or swearing aimed at a player, even once.

**What happens:**

- The first time, your chat is restricted for 1 hour.
- If you carry on, each action is stricter than the last.

For example: "loser", "you're an idiot", "go f— yourself".

### Bullying

**What counts:** Sustained or repeated aggression: several insults, picking a fight, following someone across games.

**What happens:**

- The first time, your chat is restricted for 24 hours.

For example: "three insults in one game", "insulting the same player again next game".

### After a warning

**What counts:** Carrying on after you have been warned.

**What happens:**

- If you carry on after a warning, the next step is at least a chat timeout of 24 hours. It gets stricter each time, up to a permanent ban.

### Severe

**What counts:** Threats, hate or slurs, attacks on who someone is, sexual harassment, doxxing, serious harassment.

**What happens:**

- The first time, you are banned for 7 days.
- This is acted on straight away, whatever your record.

For example: "any slur", "I'll find you".

### Some rules work differently

A chat timeout is a ban from public rooms and matchmaking instead when you break CR 5 (No cheating or exploiting) or CR 6 (No throwing, stalling or ruining games on purpose).

Breaking CR 1 (No slurs or hate aimed at who someone is) is always treated as serious, whatever your record.

## Swearing

Messages with swear words are not sent, and you will see a message when that happens. Swearing on its own is never a reason for action. Aiming abuse at a player is covered by the rules above.

## How to report

Use the report option in the game. Pick the reason that fits best and describe what happened. Recent chat from that game is reviewed before a decision is made.

Only report real problems. If the moderators decide not to act on a report, that is not a problem for you. Reports made on purpose to get someone in trouble can mean you lose the ability to report.

## If you get a notice

If you are warned or restricted, you will see a notice. It shows the rule number (for example, CR 1) and a reference code that starts with M-. Keep the code: you will need it if you contact us about the decision.

## Think it's a mistake?

If you think a decision was a mistake, [contact the moderators](https://example.com/appeals) and quote the reference code from your notice.
"
`;

exports[`every document, every preset > strict > snapshot: moderator guide (markdown) 1`] = `
"# Moderator guide: Strict

Be kind. No swearing, insults or bullying.

This guide is generated from the moderation profile and the Community Rules in force, so it matches what the kit enforces. It is for the moderation team: do not publish it.

## Community Rules

- **CR 1. No slurs or hate aimed at who someone is**: Do not use slurs, or put someone down for their race, religion, gender, sexuality, disability or similar. This applies to what you say about other players and about anyone else.
- **CR 2. No insulting, threatening or targeting another player**: Do not insult, swear at, threaten or target another player in chat. Talking about the game itself is fine; aiming it at a person is not.
- **CR 3. No sexual messages**: Do not send sexual messages or comments, and do not pressure anyone for them.
- **CR 4. No spam, flooding or advertising**: Do not repeat the same message, flood the chat or advertise. Stick to talking about the game and the people in it.
- **CR 5. No cheating or exploiting**: Do not cheat, or use a bug or loophole to get an unfair edge. Report bugs instead of using them.
- **CR 6. No throwing, stalling or ruining games on purpose**: Do not lose on purpose, stall the game or leave a game running just to spoil it for others. Play to finish, or concede.
- **CR 7. No offensive names**: Do not pick a name that breaks any other rule here, such as a slur, a sexual name or a name aimed at another player.
- **CR 8. No false reports**: Do not report someone to get them in trouble when they have not broken a rule. Use reports for real problems.

## Conduct levels

| Level | Meaning | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| banter | Friendly salt and jokes about play, with no insults and no swearing | ez; gg; bad play; lol |
| rude | Any insult or swearing aimed at a player, even once | loser; you're an idiot; go f— yourself |
| hostile | Sustained or repeated aggression: several insults, picking a fight, following someone across games | three insults in one game; insulting the same player again next game |
| severe | Threats, hate or slurs, attacks on who someone is, sexual harassment, doxxing, serious harassment | any slur; I'll find you; anything about race or religion as an attack |

## Our guidelines

### Banter

Friendly salt and jokes about play, with no insults. Swearing that is not aimed at anyone is stopped before it is sent, and that is not a violation.

Examples: ez; gg; bad play; lol

Covers: banter

Outcome: No action. Nothing is recorded.

### Rudeness

Any insult or swearing aimed at a player, even once. Any earlier note on the record makes it repeated.

Examples: loser; you're an idiot; go f— yourself

Covers: rude, repeated behaviour

Outcome: First time: chat restricted for 1 hour. Repeated (any earlier note on the record): chat restricted for 24 hours.

### Bullying

Several insults, picking a fight, or aggression that continues across games.

Examples: three insults in one game; insulting the same player again next game

Covers: hostile

Outcome: Chat restricted for 24 hours.

### After a warning

The behaviour continues after the player has been warned.

Covers: after a warning

Outcome: Longer restrictions, then bans, stepping up with each action.

### Severe

Threats, hate or slurs, attacks on who someone is, sexual harassment, doxxing and other serious harassment.

Examples: any slur; I'll find you

Covers: severe

Outcome: A 7 day ban at once.

## First offense

What a person with a clean record gets for each level.

| Level | Outcome |
| --- | --- |
| banter | No action |
| rude | Restrict chat 1 hour |
| hostile | Restrict chat 24 hours |
| severe | Full ban 7 days |

Banter is never acted on, whatever the record.

## Repeated behaviour

1 note in 30 days counts as repeated: Restrict chat 24 hours.

Repeated applies while the person has no warning or restriction on record; once they do, the ladder below applies. At least one earlier note is always needed. Revoked notes, and notes older than the window, do not count. An escalation is never milder than the first-offense outcome.

## Escalation ladder

A person's step is the heaviest action on their record in the last 90 days. Step 0 is notes only, 1 is a warning, 2 is a chat or area restriction under 7 days (or two warnings), 3 is a restriction of 7 days or more or a ban under 7 days, 4 is a ban of 7 to 29 days, 5 is a ban of 30 days or more or anything permanent.

| Step | Low / medium (banter, rude) | High (hostile with a record, severe) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Warning | Restrict chat 7 days |
| 1 | Restrict chat 24 hours | Restrict chat 7 days |
| 2 | Restrict chat 7 days | Full ban 7 days |
| 3 | Full ban 7 days | Full ban 30 days |
| 4 | Full ban 30 days | Full ban permanent |
| 5 | Full ban permanent | Full ban permanent |

Rules that turn a chat restriction into a ban from public rooms and matchmaking at the same length: CR 5. No cheating or exploiting; CR 6. No throwing, stalling or ruining games on purpose.

Rules that always read the High column: CR 1. No slurs or hate aimed at who someone is.

## The AI read

The AI may act on its own for: hostile, severe. It never acts on its own for banter or rude; a moderator decides those.

## Profanity

- A message with swearing is refused before it is sent.
- Word lists: en.
- The profanity filter never creates a strike, note, sanction or notice. Swearing aimed at a player is still judged as rude.

## Writing a reason

Write the reason in your own words: what was said, and why it breaks the rule you cite. The reason is for the record. The player never sees it, only the rule number and a reference code.

## Dismissing a report

A dismissed report is not bad faith; bad faith needs evidence. Use no\\_action when a report does not hold up. Use bad\\_faith only when you can write down the evidence of deliberate abuse of the report tool (for example, reports made to get someone in trouble when no rule was broken), and then only as the evidence shows.

## Rule gaps

When no Community Rule fits what happened, cite "uncovered" and write a rule-gap note: what happened, and which rule would have covered it. Gap notes are reviewed together; each is closed as a new rule or as not a rule.

## What is private

Notes are private. A note is a record for moderators only: the player is not told, and it restricts nothing. The reason you write, a rule-gap note, the reporter and any AI output are private too.
"
`;
